# Universe Schema

**Version:** 1.0

**Status:** Draft

**Owner:** Headcanon Core Engine

---

# 1. Purpose

The Universe Schema defines the canonical structure of every Headcanon universe.

It is the **single source of truth** for every engine within the Headcanon ecosystem.

Every imported story is transformed into one Universe object.

Once created, every engine—including Character Engine, Simulation Engine, Scene Engine, Memory Engine and Media Pipeline—operates using this Universe instead of the original story.

The original story becomes an import source only.

The Universe becomes the persistent representation of that fictional world.

---

# 2. Design Principles

The Universe follows several strict architectural principles.

## 2.1 Single Source of Truth

Every piece of canonical information should exist exactly once.

Example:

Hermione's personality is stored once.

Other engines reference it.

They never duplicate it.

---

## 2.2 Immutable Canon

The Universe represents the reconstructed canonical world.

User interactions never directly modify the Universe.

Instead they modify the World State.

---

## 2.3 Separation of Concerns

The Universe stores permanent information.

The World State stores temporary information.

Example

Universe

```
Hermione

Personality

Speech Style

Background
```

World State

```
Hermione

Current Location

Current Emotion

Current Goal

Inventory

Current Action
```

---

## 2.4 ID-Based References

Every entity is referenced by ID.

Never by name.

Correct

```
char_harry
```

Incorrect

```
Harry Potter
```

Names can change.

IDs never do.

---

## 2.5 No Duplicate Information

Characters never duplicate location data.

Objects never duplicate owner information.

Relationships never duplicate character information.

Everything references IDs.

---

## 2.6 Serializable

Every Universe must be stored as JSON.

No runtime objects.

No Python-specific structures.

No circular references.

---

## 2.7 Engine Independence

Every engine consumes the same Universe.

No engine defines additional schema fields.

If new fields are required,

the Universe Schema must evolve first.

---

# 3. Universe Object

Every imported story becomes exactly one Universe.

Structure

```json
{
  "metadata": {},
  "characters": [],
  "locations": [],
  "objects": [],
  "relationships": [],
  "timeline": [],
  "world_rules": [],
  "knowledge_graph": {},
  "world_state": {}
}
```

Field descriptions

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|--------|------|----------|-------------|
| metadata | Object | Yes | Story metadata |
| characters | Array | Yes | Canonical character definitions |
| locations | Array | Yes | World locations |
| objects | Array | Yes | Physical objects |
| relationships | Array | Yes | Character relationships |
| timeline | Array | Yes | Canonical events |
| world_rules | Array | Yes | Immutable universe rules |
| knowledge_graph | Object | Yes | Entity graph |
| world_state | Object | Yes | Initial world state |

---

# 4. Metadata Schema

Metadata identifies the imported universe.

Example

```json
{
    "id":"hp_001",

    "title":"Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone",

    "author":"J. K. Rowling",

    "source":"PDF",

    "language":"English",

    "genre":[
        "Fantasy",
        "Adventure"
    ],

    "created_at":"2026-08-01T09:15:00Z",

    "schema_version":"1.0"
}
```

Field descriptions

### id

Unique universe identifier.

Must never change.

Example

```
hp_001
```

---

### title

Original story title.

---

### author

Story author.

If unknown

```
Unknown
```

---

### source

Import source.

Allowed values

```
PDF

EPUB

TXT

Markdown

AO3

Wattpad

Project Gutenberg

Custom
```

---

### language

ISO language.

Example

```
English
```

---

### genre

Array of genres.

Example

```json
[
    "Fantasy",
    "Adventure"
]
```

---

### created_at

UTC timestamp.

Never local time.

---

### schema_version

Current Universe Schema version.

Example

```
1.0
```

