# 7. Location Schema

Locations define every explorable place inside the universe.

Locations are immutable definitions.

The World State determines who is currently inside them.

Structure

```json
{
    "id":"",

    "name":"",

    "description":"",

    "type":"",

    "connected_locations":[],

    "objects":[],

    "metadata":{}
}
```

---

## id

Unique location identifier.

Format

```
loc_<name>
```

Examples

```
loc_great_hall

loc_library

loc_hogsmeade
```

---

## name

Canonical location name.

Example

```
Great Hall
```

---

## description

Permanent description.

Example

```
A vast dining hall beneath an enchanted ceiling.
```

Descriptions should not include temporary information.

Incorrect

```
Harry is sitting here.
```

Correct

```
The main dining hall of Hogwarts.
```

---

## type

Examples

```
Building

Room

City

Village

Forest

Castle

Dungeon

Planet

Spacecraft
```

---

## connected_locations

Defines navigable paths.

Example

```json
[
    "loc_library",
    "loc_corridor",
    "loc_staircase"
]
```

Simulation uses these connections for movement.

---

## objects

Canonical objects belonging to this location.

Example

```json
[
    "obj_sorting_hat",
    "obj_teacher_table"
]
```

Ownership is handled by World State.

---

## Location Validation

Every location must satisfy

✓ Unique ID

✓ Name exists

✓ Description exists

✓ Every connected location exists

✓ No duplicate connections

✓ No circular self references

