# 11. World Rules Schema

World Rules define the immutable laws governing the fictional universe.

Unlike timeline events, these rules are **always true** unless the source material explicitly changes them.

Simulation Engine, Character Engine, and Interaction Engine must always respect these rules.

Structure

```json
{
    "id":"",

    "title":"",

    "description":"",

    "category":"",

    "immutable":true,

    "metadata":{}
}
```

---

## id

Format

```
rule_<name>
```

Examples

```
rule_magic_requires_wand

rule_force_sensitive

rule_pokemon_capture
```

---

## title

Human-readable rule name.

Example

```
Magic Requires Magical Ability
```

---

## description

Explain the rule clearly.

Example

```
Only witches and wizards possessing magical ability may naturally cast spells.
```

---

## category

Examples

```
Magic

Physics

Combat

Politics

Religion

Technology

Biology

Social
```

---

## immutable

Always true for imported canon.

Example

```json
true
```

Only the Universe Builder may create or remove world rules.

---

## Rule Validation

Every rule must satisfy

✓ Unique ID

✓ Category exists

✓ Description exists

✓ Immutable field exists

✓ No duplicate rules

---

# World Rule Philosophy

Rules define **how the universe works**.

Characters may violate laws.

They cannot violate world rules.

Example

Harry can break school rules.

Harry cannot suddenly breathe underwater unless canon permits it.

---

