# 18. Summary

The Universe Schema is the canonical specification for every Headcanon universe.

It defines **what exists**, **how entities are represented**, and **how they relate to one another**, while remaining independent of runtime gameplay.

The Universe is intentionally **mostly immutable**. User interactions never rewrite canon directly; instead, they operate on the separate World State.

Every engine in Headcanon—Universe Builder, Character Engine, Simulation Engine, Timeline Engine, Scene Engine, Media Pipeline, and any future systems—must consume and produce data that conforms to this schema.

Any change to the Universe Schema is an architectural change and must be versioned before implementation.